     ddeeffaauullttddoommaaiinn — default YP domain name

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeeffaauullttddoommaaiinn file is read by rc(8) at system startup time.  It is
     used to set the YP domain name of the host machine (see yp(8)).

     This file should contain a single line specifying the system domain name
     as supplied to domainname(1).  Empty lines and lines beginning with ‘#’
     in the file are ignored.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/defaultdomain  default domain name

